## Simulated Data Test (NEW)

200 patients × 5 visits with **known true parameters**:
`outcome = 20 + 1.0·time + 2.0·Male + 0.5·time·groupB + 1.0·time·groupC + b0 + b1·time + e`,
with b0 ~ N(0, 2²), b1 ~ N(0, 0.5²), e ~ N(0, 1.5²).
`biomarker` is log-normal and related to the patient intercept b0. `Sex` and `group` are time-invariant.

The test fits the same mixed model to the simulated "real" data and to the synthetic data and compares
the estimates with the truth: the conclusions should transfer.

```{r sim-data}
simulate_longitudinal <- function(n_patients = 200, n_timepoints = 5, seed = 2026) {
  set.seed(seed)
  patients <- tibble(
    patient_id = sprintf("P%03d", seq_len(n_patients)),
    Sex   = factor(sample(c("Male", "Female"), n_patients, replace = TRUE), levels = c("Male", "Female")),
    group = factor(sample(c("A", "B", "C"), n_patients, replace = TRUE)),
    b0 = rnorm(n_patients, 0, 2),
    b1 = rnorm(n_patients, 0, 0.5)
  )
  patients %>%
    crossing(time = seq_len(n_timepoints)) %>%
    mutate(
      outcome = 20 + 1.0 * time + 2.0 * (Sex == "Male") +
                0.5 * time * (group == "B") + 1.0 * time * (group == "C") +
                b0 + b1 * time + rnorm(n(), 0, 1.5),
      biomarker = exp(1 + 0.15 * b0 + 0.05 * time + rnorm(n(), 0, 0.3))
    ) %>%
    select(patient_id, time, outcome, biomarker, Sex, group)
}

sim_data <- simulate_longitudinal()
head(sim_data)
